cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use scanlib in your work, please cite it as below, together with
  the published methods behind the functions you use.
title: scanlib
abstract: >-
  One-dimensional scanning astrometry: the along-scan instrument model, the
  back-projection map of the detections, the inverse Radon transform and
  faststack images of the windows, and the joint window-level likelihood
  fit, with the paper's pipeline built from them (the per-window reduction,
  the fits to the detections, the campaign threshold and the search).
  Arrays in, results out.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahaf
    given-names: Sahar
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/saharsh1/scanlib
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - astrometry
  - scanning
  - Gaia
  - imaging
  - back-projection
